00:50:31,578 --> 00:50:37,578
Blood: The Last Vampire (stylized in all caps) is a 2000 Japanese animated action horror film directed by Hiroyuki Kitakubo and written
by Kenji Kamiyama; the film is created by Production I.G, who also produced the film alongside their IG Plus division.

11
00:55:34,736 --> 00:55:40,736
Distributed by Sony Pictures Entertainment, a girl named Saya (Youki Kudoh), who hunts the hematophagous-bat-like
creatures called Chiropterans, is tasked to eliminate the creatures at Yokota Air Base by her handlers.

12
01:00:37,894 --> 01:00:43,894
Blood: The Last Vampire first premiered at Fantasia International Film
Festival on July 27, 2000, and later in Japan on November 18.

13
01:05:41,052 --> 01:05:47,052
Manga Entertainment licensed the film and released it theatrically in the United
States in Summer 2001, and later on August 3 through home media release.

14
01:10:44,210 --> 01:10:50,210
Blood: The Last Vampire spawned a sequel manga, three light
novels and a video game from 2001 to 2006.

15
01:15:47,368 --> 01:15:53,368
It also spawned two anime series: Blood+, which aired
from 2005 to 2006, and Blood-C in 2011.

16
01:20:50,526 --> 01:20:56,526
A live-action film adaptation with the same title was released in 2009.

17
01:25:53,684 --> 01:25:59,684
The film explores themes of vampire, sexploitation, slasher,
nazisploitation (nazi exploitation film).

18
01:30:56,842 --> 01:31:02,842
The tone is dark and intense.
